# `T-4` (tflw `D1373`) — LOAD's view of this project's own workload file after a `--workers 1` run
# (`tests/load/shapes.tflw`, five shapes): the run is started under the LOAD chip with one worker,
# and the report it keeps holds each workload as a row of the run's tree; the one picked draws its
# shape, its charts, and every threshold with its verdict. The run takes as long as its shapes do,
# so the waits are the workload's length.

test "a workload run under the LOAD chip draws its shapes, its charts and its thresholds' verdicts"
  let token = env(TFLW_UI_TOKEN)
  open "/?token={token}#/run?kind=load"
  expect css "[data-runstrip]" is visible
  fill css "[data-search]" with "tests/load/shapes.tflw"
  # `workers` sits in the header's `more…` since tflw `M254` (`D1400`).
  click css "[data-run-more] summary"
  fill css "[data-workers]" with "1"
  click css "[data-run]"
  # Five workloads, five rows in the run's tree — one per test in the file (tflw `D1409`).
  wait until css "[data-report] [data-tree-test]" has count 5 timeout wait 180s
  # The tree draws one test at a time; a name in its filter opens the group the test is in.
  fill css "[data-filter-text]" with "a ramp reaches its target concurrency"
  click css "[data-tree-test][data-name=\"a ramp reaches its target concurrency and the catalogue keeps answering\"]"
  expect css "[data-report] [data-workload-shape]" has count 1
  expect css "[data-report] [data-chart]" has count at least 1
  expect css "[data-report] [data-threshold]" has count at least 1
